# Leading and driving in Russian: веду, везу
subtitle: "Веду́ or везу́? Take a friend to the Hermitage on foot or by taxi, and learn why вожу́ can mean both."
tags: ["russian","verbs of motion","вести везти","russian grammar","hermitage"]
teaches: ["grammar/verbs-of-motion","vocabulary/the-city"]
thumb: "band \"One letter: car or on foot\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Oneself in Russian: себя, сам, свой","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/115-russian-oneself.cast"}

## Leading and driving in Russian: веду, везу
